author ai
group index
note The in-memory shape of the auto layer: what an indexed repo is, in the domain crate with no I/O. One Index per process holds one SourceFile per text file under the root, each SourceFile holds its lines, its per-line highlight spans, its imports and its Symbols, and each Symbol holds the raw material for xrefs plus the resolved callee and caller lists. Nothing here is persisted as truth: the whole thing is rebuilt from disk and the cache at startup. Symbols are addressed by SymbolId, a pair of positions, which is fast but only valid until the next re-index; anything that has to survive one uses SymbolKey, the (file path, symbol name) pair, instead.

